    description: "Found in DEEP bakeoff deep-20260623-134237 cohort-001 iter-004 (sherpa-csharp). 'new WaveReader(...)' instantiation edges land their in-degree on the CLASS node (WaveReader in-degree 24) rather than the constructor node (WaveReader.WaveReader in-degree 1). A reverse slice seeded on the constructor therefore returns only 2 nodes and misses ~24 real construction call sites — crippling refactoring-safety analysis ('who constructs this?'). The class node conflates 'referenced as a type' with 'instantiated'. Evidence: reflect/cohort-001/iter-004/sherpa-csharp.assessment.yaml; rslice on WaveReader.WaveReader = 2 nodes vs class in-degree 24."  # 9f41
